Voiceover

Once operational recommendations have been generated, finance leadership requires a consolidated view of the organization’s overall accrual position.
The Executive Summary dashboard brings together key financial indicators into a single view, providing immediate visibility into the organization’s accrual health.
Key metrics such as Total Accrual Exposure, PO Accrual Completeness, Predicted Period-End Accrual, Open Accrual Items, and Exposure by Aging Bucket help leadership understand the current financial position and identify potential areas of concern.
Rather than waiting until month-end reconciliation is complete, finance teams can continuously monitor accrual performance, identify emerging risks early, and make informed decisions before the financial close process begins.
This enables better financial governance, increased visibility, and faster executive decision-making.
SLIDE 3 – Trends & Spikes (Historical Analysis)
Visual Focus

•	Open the Trends & Spikes dashboard.
•	Highlight the rolling trend chart.
•	Move to Month-over-Month Variance.
•	Highlight Exposure Distribution.
•	End with Average Days Open by Worklist Category.
Voiceover

Understanding today’s accrual position is important, but understanding how it changes over time provides even greater business value.
The Trends & Spikes dashboard analyses historical accrual data across multiple accounting periods to identify long-term trends, seasonal patterns, and unusual fluctuations.
Finance teams can quickly detect sudden increases in accrual exposure, compare month-over-month performance, and investigate significant variances before they become financial reporting issues.
Operational metrics such as Average Days Open by Worklist Category also provide insight into process efficiency by measuring how quickly different types of accrual cases are resolved.
These historical insights support continuous process improvement and enable more proactive financial management throughout the accounting cycle.
SLIDE 4 – Vendor Intelligence (Supplier Risk Analysis)
Visual Focus

•	Open Vendor Intelligence dashboard.
•	Highlight Vendor Exposure vs Invoice Delay chart.
•	Move to Top Suppliers by Age of Un-Invoiced Receipts.
•	Highlight Predicted Unrecorded Liabilities.
•	End with Supplier Contribution and Exposure Index visuals.
Voiceover

Supplier behaviour has a direct impact on accrual accuracy and financial risk.
The Vendor Intelligence dashboard provides supplier-level insights by analysing invoice delays, ageing of uninvoiced receipts, predicted unrecorded liabilities, supplier exposure indices, and historical spending patterns.
Machine learning identifies suppliers demonstrating unusual behaviour and highlights potential risks before they affect the period-end financial close.
These insights allow finance and procurement teams to proactively engage with suppliers, prioritize high-risk transactions, improve accrual accuracy, and reduce unexpected financial adjustments.
By combining operational data with predictive intelligence, organizations gain a deeper understanding of supplier performance and strengthen overall financial control.
SLIDE 5 – AI & Solution Architecture
Visual Focus

•	Display the end-to-end architecture diagram.
•	Highlight SAP S/4HANA as the source system.
•	Show the flow through Datasphere, Databricks, AI models, and SAC dashboards.
•	End by highlighting the business user interface.
Voiceover

The solution is built on SAP Business Data Cloud and combines multiple SAP technologies into a unified analytics platform.
Transactional data is extracted from SAP S/4HANA and integrated through SAP Datasphere, where it is prepared and harmonized for downstream processing.
Databricks performs advanced data engineering and machine learning, generating intelligent accrual recommendations and predictive insights.
These results are presented through SAP Analytics Cloud dashboards, providing finance users with operational worklists, executive reporting, trend analysis, and vendor intelligence in a single integrated solution.
This architecture ensures scalability, transparency, and seamless integration with the existing SAP landscape while enabling AI-driven financial decision-making.
